{"evidence":{"id":"E1","kind":"fact","text":"revenue for fiscal year ending 2012-12-31 = $1,834.9M (XBRL tag SalesRevenueGoodsNet)","source":"10-K accession 0001336917-13-000011, filed 2013-02-25"},"origins":{"queries":[{"sql":"SELECT * FROM veritas_pg.facts WHERE cik = 1336917 ORDER BY fy_end, CASE concept WHEN 'revenue' THEN 0 WHEN 'cogs' THEN 1 WHEN 'sga' THEN 2 WHEN 'depreciation' THEN 3 WHEN 'net_income' THEN 4 WHEN 'cfo' THEN 5 WHEN 'receivables' THEN 6 WHEN 'current_assets' THEN 7 WHEN 'ppe' THEN 8 WHEN 'assets' THEN 9 WHEN 'current_liabilities' THEN 10 WHEN 'lt_debt' THEN 11 ELSE 99 END","rows":[{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2012-12-31","concept":"revenue","tag":"SalesRevenueGoodsNet","value":"1834921000","accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25"}],"mode":"zetaris","label":"executed on Zetaris","table":"facts"}],"rows":[{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2012-12-31","concept":"revenue","tag":"SalesRevenueGoodsNet","value":"1834921000","accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2013-12-31","activeRevision":"7d3e957400e5","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0001336917-13-000011","filed":"2013-02-25","cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1336917/000133691713000011/0001336917-13-000011-index.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":0,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue growth driven by $176.8M (33.2%) increase in direct-to-consumer sales (18 new stores, ecommerce) and $10.2M (22.8%) license revenue growth.","numbers_show":"Total revenue grew $497.2M (27.1%). Cited drivers sum to $187M, covering only 37.6% of growth. The remaining ~$310M (wholesale) is unexplained in the provided MD&A. Receivables grew 19.6% vs revenue 27.1%; DSO improved 35→33 days annually, but quarterly DSO worsened in Q1 (46→48) and improved sharply in Q4 (32→28). Operating cash flow dropped 40% ($199.8M→$120.1M) while net income rose 26%.","fit":"does not fit","evidence":["E13","E1","E32","E33","E34","E35","E25","E27","E30","E26"],"verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue growth of $497.2M (27.1%) was primarily driven by a $176.8M (33.2%) increase in direct-to-consumer sales from 18 new retail stores and ecommerce growth, plus a $10.2M (22.8%) increase in license revenues.","numbers_show":"Revenue grew 27.1% ($1,834.9M to $2,332.1M). Direct-to-consumer growth accounts for ~35.5% of total growth. Receivables grew only 19.6% ($175.5M to $210.0M) and DSO improved from 35 to 33 days. Quarter-level signals show DSO improvements in Q3 (49→44) and Q4 (32→28), consistent with a higher proportion of cash-based direct-to-consumer sales.","fit":"fits","evidence":["E1","E13","E25","E27","E28","E29","E30","E34","E35"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}}],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":0,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"does not fit","reason":"Management's stated drivers (DTC +$176.8M, license +$10.2M) sum to $187M, covering only 37.6% of the $497.2M revenue increase. The remaining ~$310M is not attributed to any driver in the provided MD&A. Segment data (E55) shows North America revenue grew $467M but does not break out wholesale vs DTC; the MD&A links North America growth to the same consolidated drivers, not providing a separate wholesale driver.","evidence":["E1","E13","E32","E33","E34","E35","E55"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"The $310M of revenue growth not attributed to DTC or license channels is wholesale revenue within the North America segment, which grew $467.0M (E55) and, combined with $30.1M international growth (E55), accounts for the total $497.2M increase (E13, E1). The MD&A states North America growth was \"primarily due to the items discussed above in the Consolidated Results of Operations\" (E55), linking it to the same demand drivers. The quarterly DSO patterns (E27-E30) reflect seasonal shipment timing (Q4 revenue surge 35% with DSO improving to 28 days) rather than collection deterioration.","evidence":["E13","E1","E55","E27","E28","E29","E30"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers","confidence":0.82}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":1,"rulingIndex":3,"finding_index":3,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Gross margin improved 80 bps (47.9% to 48.7%) per MD&A and computed from revenue/COGS (E1, E2, E13, E14, E35). However, the causal drivers—60 bps from sales mix shift and 50 bps from lower input costs—are not independently visible in the numbers. Segment data is geographic (E55), not by channel (DTC vs wholesale), and input costs are not disclosed. The explanation rests on management's word.","evidence":["E1","E2","E13","E14","E35","E36","E37"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":3,"innocent_explanation":"Gross margin improved 80 bps due to a favorable sales mix shift toward higher-margin DTC channels and lower apparel input costs, as reported by management.","evidence":["E1","E2","E13","E14","E35","E36","E37"],"support":"management's word"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.78}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"fits","reason":"Revenue growth of 27.1% matches MD&A reported direct-to-consumer growth of $176.8M (33.2%) and license growth of $10.2M (22.8%), together accounting for 37.6% of total revenue increase. Receivables grew slower (19.6%) and DSO improved from 35 to 33 days, with quarter-level DSO improvements in Q3 (49→44) and Q4 (32→28) consistent with a shift to cash-based direct-to-consumer sales.","evidence":["E1","E13","E25","E27","E28","E29","E30","E34","E35"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"The 27.1% revenue growth was driven by a 33.2% increase in direct-to-consumer sales ($176.8M) and 22.8% license revenue growth ($10.2M), which together account for a substantial portion of the $497.2M total increase. The slower receivables growth (19.6%) and DSO improvement (35 to 33 days) are consistent with a shift toward cash-based direct-to-consumer sales, as shown by quarter-level DSO improvements in Q3 (49→44) and Q4 (32→28).","evidence":["E1","E13","E34","E35","E25","E27","E28","E29","E30"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":1,"finding_index":1,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Gross margin improved 80 bps, but the named drivers (sales mix shift away from excess inventory/wholesale footwear, and lower input costs) are not directly visible in the reported numbers. The MD&A attributes 60 bps to sales mix and 50 bps to input costs, but the evidence pack lacks channel-level gross margins or input cost data to corroborate the magnitude. Receivables DSO improvement is consistent with a channel shift but does not quantify the gross margin impact.","evidence":["E36","E37","E25","E29","E30","E1","E2","E13","E14"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":1,"innocent_explanation":"Gross margin improved 80 basis points (from 47.9% to 48.7%) due to a favorable sales mix shift away from lower-margin wholesale/outlet sales toward higher-margin direct-to-consumer channels, supported by the DSO improvement, and lower North American apparel/accessories input costs.","evidence":["E1","E2","E13","E14","E36","E37","E25","E29","E30"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2013-12-31","revisionId":"7d3e957400e5","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":3,"finding_index":3,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"The Beneish M-score of -1.7072 flags potential manipulation risk, but the high AQI (2.27) and SGI (1.27) are driven by legitimate high sales growth (27.1%) and asset growth (36.3%). The numbers do not distinguish between manipulation and high growth.","evidence":["E31","E1","E13","E10","E22"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":3,"innocent_explanation":"The Beneish M-score of -1.7072 (flagged above -1.78) is driven by high sales growth (SGI=1.27) and asset growth (AQI=2.27) from legitimate business expansion, not earnings manipulation; revenue grew 27.1% and total assets grew 36.3% year-over-year.","evidence":["E31","E1","E13","E10","E22"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}}],"audit":[{"seq":1,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E1 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":10,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E10 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":11,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E11 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":12,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E12 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":13,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E13 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":14,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E14 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":15,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E15 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":16,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E16 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":17,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2013-12-31:7d3e957400e5:E17 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":18,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336